# γ-FeOOH lepidocrocite, space group Cmcm (No. 63)
# Lattice & Fe / O(2) sites: Zhukhlistov (2001) electron-diffraction
#   refinement, as tabulated in Guo & Barnard, PCCP 14 (2012) 3306
#   (Table 2, ED column): a=3.072, b=12.516, c=3.873 A;
#   Fe (0.5, 0.1778, 0.25); O(2) (0, 0.2889, 0.25)
# O(1) site completed geometrically at (0, 0.0667, 0.25): the ED O(1)
#   listing (y~0.00, 4c) leaves the FeO6 octahedron open (only 4 bonds,
#   all on one side of Fe) and is presumed garbled in the source table.
#   The completed site closes all octahedra:
#   Fe-O = 1.98 A x2 (axial OH) + 2.07 A x4 (equatorial);
#   Fe-Fe = 3.06 x4 + 3.07 x2 (edge-sharing) + 3.87 x2 (corner-sharing),
#   matching published EXAFS values for gamma-FeOOH.
data_lepidocrocite_gamma_FeOOH
_cell_length_a 3.072
_cell_length_b 12.516
_cell_length_c 3.873
_cell_angle_alpha 90
_cell_angle_beta 90
_cell_angle_gamma 90
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'C m c m'
loop_
_atom_site_label
_atom_site_type_symbol
_atom_site_fract_x
_atom_site_fract_y
_atom_site_fract_z
Fe1 Fe 0.5000 0.1778 0.2500
O1  O  0.0000 0.0667 0.2500
O2  O  0.0000 0.2889 0.2500
